---

<PageLayout title="“Emin Semsuğ” (Biyografi.Net)">
  <p>
    <a href="/people/amin-samkough/">&larr; Amin Samkough</a> &middot;
    <a href="/people/amin-samkough/research/">Research</a>
  </p>
  <hr />

  <section id="details">
    <h2>About this page</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Article</dt>
      <dd>
        <span lang="tr">«Emin Semsuğ»</span> (“Emin Semsuğ”), a biographical
        entry
      </dd>
      <dt>Website</dt>
      <dd>
        <span lang="tr">Biyografi.Net</span>, a Turkish biography directory
      </dd>
      <dt>Author</dt>
      <dd>None given (the page’s author field is empty)</dd>
      <dt>Published</dt>
      <dd>
        <strong>No date is shown on the page.</strong> The earliest copy I can
        find in the Internet Archive is from
        <time datetime="2025-02-19">19 February 2025</time>. The text itself
        was published earlier: on
        <time datetime="2019-03-22">22 March 2019</time> by Circassian Center,
        and with a date of
        <time datetime="2009-12-08">8 December 2009</time> on
        <a href="/people/amin-samkough/research/bilgiler-emin-semsug/">Bilgiler</a>
        (see below).
      </dd>
      <dt>Source</dt>
      <dd>
        <a href={sourceUrl}>{sourceUrl}</a>
      </dd>
      <dt>Language</dt>
      <dd>Turkish</dd>
    </dl>
    <p>
      <mark>
        Review: <strong>the date.</strong> The page has no date in its text or
        in its page code, and the server gives no last-modified date either.
        The 19 February 2025 date is only the first time the Internet Archive
        saved it, so the page may be older. Later copies of it are identical.
        I would cite it as “undated, archived by 19 February 2025”, not as a
        publication date.
      </mark>
    </p>
  </section>
  <hr />

  <section id="same-text">
    <h2>This is the same text as the Circassian Center profile</h2>
    <p>
      The body of this entry is, with trivial differences, the same text as
      the
      <a href={originalUrl}>Circassian Center profile “Emin Semsuğ”</a>
      (published 22 March 2019), including the same slips and the same list
      of works. Biyografi.Net gives no credit to anyone, so it appears to be
      a copy. It is <strong>not an independent source</strong>, and the two
      web pages shouldn’t be counted as two confirmations of anything. The
      Circassian Center page has the full summary, the translated passages
      and the review items. I haven’t repeated them here.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because it is someone else’s published work, I haven’t translated it in
      full. Please have a Turkish reader check my translations.
    </p>

    <h3>What differs from the Circassian Center version</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>An added summary line</strong> at the top, giving the life dates
        and a description:
        <blockquote>
          <p lang="tr">Emin Semsuğ (1900)-(1952) yazar, yayıncı</p>
          <p>
            <em>“Emin Semsuğ (1900)–(1952), writer, publisher”</em>
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The death sentence:</strong> “1952 yılında <span lang="tr">vefat etti</span>”
        (“passed away in 1952”), where Circassian Center has
        <span lang="tr">öldü</span> (“died”). This is a more polite word for
        the same thing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No byline line.</strong> Circassian Center says “Author
        unknown”. This page gives no author either, so it doesn’t say so.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>One block of text.</strong> The paragraph breaks and the
        “Works” heading are gone, and the works list is run into the same
        paragraph.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A page image.</strong> It uses a different image from the one
        on the Circassian Center page. I haven’t reproduced either.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <hr />

  <section id="review">
    <h2>Things to review</h2>
    <ul class="review">
      <li>
        <mark>
          Review: <strong>the label “writer, publisher”.</strong> Biyografi.Net
          added this, and it isn’t in the original. It leaves out his role as
          mayor and political organizer. “Publisher” (<span lang="tr">yayıncı</span>)
          presumably means his part in the newspaper <em>Marg</em>, which the
          text only says he “contributed to”. It doesn’t say he owned or edited
          it.
        </mark>
      </li>
      <li>
        <mark>
          Review: <strong>life dates.</strong> 1900–1952 here, as in the
          original. Mirzoev and the dictionary entry give 1900–1953, and the
          note on his portrait gives 1903–1952 (the
          <a href="/people/amin-samkough/biography/">biography page</a> gives
          1900–1953).
        </mark>
      </li>
      <li>
        <mark>
          Review: <strong>everything else in the original.</strong> All the
          conflicts noted on the Circassian Center page apply here word for
          word: the birthplace (Mansure), the studies in France, the 1937
          trading company against Mirzoev’s “Jolan”, the newspaper’s dates, the
          place and year of his books (Homs 1948), the school details, the
          unsourced family history and the Druze mediation. The entry has no
          references.
        </mark>
      </li>
      <li>
        <mark>
          Review: <strong>spelling.</strong> The title and summary line say
          “Semsuğ”, but the text calls his father “Semguğ”, the same mismatch
          as in the original.
        </mark>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      I corrected one thing on the Circassian Center page as a result of this
      check: its publication date is 22 March 2019, not 2020.
    </p>
  </section>
  <hr />

  <section id="translation-notes">
    <h2>Translation notes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The only new Turkish here is the one-line summary and the word
        <span lang="tr">vefat etti</span>. A Turkish reader should still
        check them.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Read the full entry in Turkish at
      <a href={sourceUrl}>biyografi.net</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

